{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-factor-measure-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0159","math_ordinal":744,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-THROUGH-S252-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Section 252N puts Lebesgue measure on the second factor R and every adjacent iterated integral denotes that measure by nu; mu remains the measure on X.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt252.tex:1015","source_normalized_sha256":"492247e1bab15272d1e53b8015c042bf6fa0cb8f23ec52cad93d6ba80dafb804","source_text":"writing \\mu for Lebesgue measure","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt252.tex:1042","target_normalized_sha256":"84eb2b123d1102b8f7c00b34116df32107cffa82d46efbac7fd9543fa7459c38","target_text":"dengan menuliskan \\nu untuk ukuran Lebesgue","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S252"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-section-measure","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0160","math_ordinal":830,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-THROUGH-S252-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Each ordinate W[{x}] is a subset of Y and its measure is the second-factor measure nu; the defining supremum on the same line already uses nu.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt252.tex:1123","source_normalized_sha256":"b0f56bd77fcf211415abd6c99791257b9b693e564e753fe8bb3720d1ae3e1845","source_text":"\\mu W[\\{x\\}]=\\sup_n\\nu(Y_n\\cap W[\\{x\\}])","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt252.tex:1157","target_normalized_sha256":"08bcddfb8984dc410d6c47f05ac646ff4c45b19fa3919ea9dfead9cfbcd9c92f","target_text":"\\nu W[\\{x\\}]=\\sup_n\\nu(Y_n\\cap W[\\{x\\}])","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S252"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-third-space-label","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0161","math_ordinal":1025,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-THROUGH-S252-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The exercise declares three spaces and immediately uses X_1 times X_2 times X_3; the third triple must begin with X_3.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt252.tex:1400","source_normalized_sha256":"d2a865327a5858a863afc7fad3010cb4fe5f9354dc3d6c9a8ddfc6e787345f75","source_text":"(X_2,\\Sigma_3,\\mu_3)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt252.tex:1433","target_normalized_sha256":"b427821373f6193bd4321b6c117f2886d6cc03b8f70e6cb3b32ed0c85fb3882b","target_text":"(X_3,\\Sigma_3,\\mu_3)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S252"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-function-subscript","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0162","math_ordinal":1346,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-THROUGH-S252-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The preceding definitions introduce Omega_f^* and Omega_g^* and the claimed symmetric-difference identity must compare those two sets.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt252.tex:1714","source_normalized_sha256":"1ff76c4d15fd420bf2ae4947f75e7f260735c44faf4ed1e8e644ee4bdd450156","source_text":"\\Omega^*\\symmdiff\\Omega^*_g","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt252.tex:1761","target_normalized_sha256":"564034f8a38b6055ebae0f17ebf15fd5d78758bd9d7b34c92e489ffe5206e8c6","target_text":"\\Omega^*_f\\symmdiff\\Omega^*_g","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S252"}
{"classification":"mathematical-malformed-integral-formula","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0163","math_ordinal":1349,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-THROUGH-S252-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The source closes math mode inside the set builder and omits the closing measure parenthesis before da. The derivative restores one typed integral; raw source atom 1350 (SHA-256 9f35ebee719b66aac436d5e685cc90901e7f56f09c007d3b971c3435571e32ea) is absorbed and explicitly ledgered as a source-math deletion in unit QA.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt252.tex:1717-1719","source_normalized_sha256":"f787d6a248f245fc4e774a310780fde62b8333f4ecbf43bf6322473e20a661ff","source_text":"premature math delimiter after \\dom g and \\mu(\\{...\\}da","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt252.tex:1764-1767","target_normalized_sha256":"8d1992bcd5247ceb41d0f2d1131cfdff24463c0c9a6600b38c631c9b68133b04","target_text":"single coherent display \\mu(\\{...\\})\\,da","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S252"}
{"classification":"mathematical-extra-opening-parenthesis","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0164","math_ordinal":996,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-THROUGH-S252-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The parallel Stieltjes term has one unmatched extra opening parenthesis; removing it restores the same averaged-endpoint form as the preceding f term.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt252.tex:1380","source_normalized_sha256":"720c938a439d6eae03ae388472cdfd93cfb862e5f8f6a72d19f5653646657226","source_text":"\\Bover12((g(x^-)+g(x^+))","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt252.tex:1413","target_normalized_sha256":"f015f758668cb3d75357b62b371e5f7e53ecfe4f47cca54d725fa3caa4cec3de","target_text":"\\Bover12(g(x^-)+g(x^+))","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S252"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-product-point-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0165","math_ordinal":446,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-THROUGH-S252-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The piecewise definition is on X times Y and the preceding branch uses both coordinates; the zero branch must quantify the other product points (x,y), not a single x alleged to lie in the product.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt252.tex:558","source_normalized_sha256":"f39b61f70da717afbe6df0832a205562ef667fe278430bc117fc223c8775a6ee","source_text":"x\\in X\\times Y","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt252.tex:576","target_normalized_sha256":"84f78927f9e45ae6c6e724dd73be84255649088e60fc27237025467dfbe03f8f","target_text":"(x,y)\\in X\\times Y","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S252"}
{"classification":"mathematical-malformed-display-delimiter","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0166","math_ordinal":584,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-THROUGH-S252-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The extra display terminator splits one inequality inside Centerline and leaves the epsilon term in mismatched math mode. The derivative restores one typed formula; raw source atom 585 (SHA-256 d755633e0e290a0c333af5abdc1b68c8b416c8093ac024f0acae09added8712e) is absorbed and explicitly ledgered as a source-math deletion in unit QA.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt252.tex:720-722","source_normalized_sha256":"f82a924a54423c5497a0d18f9e761282b7e8a2a0e22afbc22b6d9446f7745e02","source_text":"premature $$ before +\\epsilon\\sum_{i=0}^na_i","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt252.tex:739-741","target_normalized_sha256":"4a8077f996846dc2ed7b57a3099159987524057f56f1f679cde825c330accb78","target_text":"single coherent display through +\\epsilon\\sum_{i=0}^na_i","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S252"}
{"classification":"mathematical-malformed-equality-prose","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0167","math_ordinal":453,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-THROUGH-S252-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The authority places a bare equality sign after the prose predicate 'exists', yielding no left-hand operand in its second math atom. The derivative states the intended existence-and-equality claim without the orphaned sign.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt252.tex:565-566","source_normalized_sha256":"c5b718eb3065e61e0fb9cc9617def2442ba1fd3f08a2b510448f94db359f884c","source_text":"integral exists $=\\int\\tilde f_nd\\lambda$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt252.tex:583-584","target_normalized_sha256":"d02f72af7091a1b37131a813fc5300de200793db11757e2c861e32fe518e5e0f","target_text":"integral terdefinisi dan sama dengan $\\int\\tilde f_nd\\lambda$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S252"}
{"classification":"mathematical-malformed-display-delimiter","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0168","math_ordinal":838,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-THROUGH-S252-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The extra display terminator splits one defining equality inside Centerline. The derivative restores one typed formula; raw source atom 839 (SHA-256 0642bff22846e70862a8522b9d879e79327d148b0b5cf9b8a42200286f687853) is absorbed and explicitly ledgered as a source-math deletion in unit QA.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt252.tex:1137-1138","source_normalized_sha256":"f969115a3c990ef35e27821e0f3a86f1f124f4ef481f47ec0d810bcfc01e1366","source_text":"premature $$ before =\\sum_{k=1}^{4^n}","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt252.tex:1171-1172","target_normalized_sha256":"fd5336ca68bfbf7d41ebdb4c53ab2c25abc9990a0d9d85dad65c7e45baeea6b4","target_text":"single coherent display h_n(x)=\\int...=\\sum_{k=1}^{4^n}...","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S252"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-coordinate-domain","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0169","math_ordinal":1046,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-THROUGH-S252-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The domain is the plane: x and y are real coordinates while the ordered pair (x,y) lies in R^2. The derivative restores the correctly typed product point; raw source atom 1045 for the detached x (SHA-256 2d711642b726b04401627ca9fbac32f5c8530fb1903cc4db02258717921a4881) is absorbed and explicitly ledgered as a source-math deletion in unit QA.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt252.tex:1417-1418","source_normalized_sha256":"10611cde292668e4d1ba1ac5b3d1291edafe208e4b1281ca05641c465edf440d","source_text":"for other x, y\\in\\BbbR^2","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt252.tex:1450-1451","target_normalized_sha256":"1ca5c7579c75630f0ffce412a884d2c17d80e1c19448ab61c62cab9f5a605b77","target_text":"di titik (x,y)\\in\\BbbR^2 lainnya","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S252"}
